WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.450
Measure a healthy person's core
temperature through the day.

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:05.890
It is never quite the same twice.

3
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:09.310
It drifts by a few tenths
of a degree, up and down,

4
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.650
all day long.

5
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.570
Blood glucose wobbles too.

6
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.130
It rises after a meal
and falls during a fast.

7
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.900
So why is all this wobbling a sign
that control is working, not failing?

8
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.810
In this mission, you'll meet the
variables your body keeps within limits,

9
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:27.380
and the set point each one moves around.

10
00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:32.590
Then you'll build a control loop, from
receptor to coordinator to effector.

11
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:37.840
Your mission: explain why a temperature
that wobbles all day shows control working,

12
00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:38.840
not failing.
